      "source_sha256": "00591a32a85619b2997e625f2a769bb178be443f07f94fcb0763d294e4b15f0d",
      "identical_to_source": false,
      "patched": true,
      "patch_note": "Phase 6.2: the approved archive markup marks its pager with data-pagination-root / data-page-num and records server-side paging, while the copied script only looked for data-page-btn and the string \"true\". Without the fix the client pager never bound, so paging was dead on every shop archive. Phase 7.2: in server-paged mode the same function left every item hidden after a filter change, because the slice loop below it never ran; matching items are now un-hidden before the early return. Phase 8.1 added the live-search panel and the Phase 8.2 change stopped the contact handler from showing success for a submission the server had not accepted."
    },
